  "review_description": "Twenty final scientific controls passed; native reference/empty/blind GLM rewards were 1/0/1 with no exceptions. The recorded solver computed all four outputs from the supplied library. One coherent quality repair corrected a missing intensity-tolerance branch, a cross-output join and a probe annotation; original programs and failed evidence are retained. Every scientific check has an executed declared negative; the conditional additive-probe role was not needed. All 1,267 input spectra match the exact file committed beside the pinned notebook, not the changing live GNPS snapshot used by an earlier campaign. Independent solution and solver use the same matchms engine; different-engine portability, biological validity and broad factory reliability remain unproven. Symmetric matrices make pure transposition value-invariant, so no separate orientation-detection guarantee is inferred. Source licenses remain mixed, without a blanket commercial-training grant. The upstream advisory label remains unverified.",
